    "narrative": "The primary catalyst for success today is **James Wood**, who headlines our lineup with a 78.42 efficiency score. Facing Merrill Kelly and his 4.74 xERA, **James Wood** benefits from a high-upside matchup bolstered by elite xwOBA metrics and a favorable leadoff spot, making him our highest-projected asset. Similarly, **Brice Turang** earns a strong 73.40 rating against Feltner. Beyond his inherent hitting profile, **Brice Turang** is a priority start because of the specific situational synergy: a high-park-factor environment combined with a slow opposing battery that maximizes his elite sprint speed for stolen base opportunities\u2014our scarcest category. **Seiya Suzuki** also warrants attention; despite the standard projection, the combination of a favorable wind out and a 4.45 xERA arm pushes his score to 70.94, making him an anchor in the outfield.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Alex Freeland**, who posted a 43.50 score but ultimately failed to crack the starting nine. While **Alex Freeland** is trending upward, his projected position at the bottom of the order\u2014paired with the high performance floor of our active starters\u2014prevented him from displacing someone like **Henry Bolte**. Meanwhile, **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains a confirmed start at 62.07, though his inclusion carries a specific 38% rain risk flag; we will monitor this closely, as any delay could jeopardize his ability to accumulate counting stats. While **Zach McKinstry** was considered, his 38.03 score fell well below our \"Zebras Floor,\" and he remains benched to preserve our limited game caps for the more efficient **Corbin Carroll** and **Tyler Soderstrom**. Ensure we remain vigilant regarding the lineup status of **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, and **Brice Turang**, as their final positional assignments could slightly shift our daily efficiency outlook.",
